      "text": "Cocora Valley and a Coffee Farm"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "efc8547c69c02921f5a6f3a262655a567b6f6252fef7d55257394ddf94f5bd5f",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-chat-20261110-0451-41d9d0b7bf00",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, we head to the Cocora Valley in Los Nevados National Park.\n\nThe region is known for its biodiversity and its wax palms, the tallest in the world. The wax palm is Colombia's national tree, and its resin was once used to make candles.\n\nThese palms grow in the Andes at elevations above 3,000 metres. Around 2,000 trees remain.\n\nAfter walking through the valley, you'll have time for lunch. **Lunch is not included.**\n\nWe then transfer to Salento, a small town with colourful houses and inviting streets. After walking around town, we take a Willys Jeep to a coffee farm.\n\nAt the farm, you'll see how coffee is made, from planting seedlings and picking cherries to processing, drying and roasting the beans. The visit also takes in the processing plant.\n\nThe tour ends with a coffee tasting.\n\nReturn to the hotel.\n\n**Duration:** 8 hours.\n\n**Included:** admission to the places listed, a bilingual guide, private transport, a local medical assistance card and a canelazo tasting."
    },
